      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Paublillo",
          "subtitle": "Colombian Trick Game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Paublillo is a Colombian trick-taking game from Tolima. 2-8 players (best 6), 40-card Spanish deck. Three-card hands, betting; win at least two of three tricks. Trump 4 (monja) and 3 (paublillo) are special. 12 stones to win."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tolima department, Colombia. Mostly rural; farmers, fishermen. Little presence in IbaguÃ©; unknown in BogotÃ¡. Based on Felipe Sanchez Vidales."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2, 4, 6, or 8. Best 6. Teams of equal size; each player between two opponents."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "40-card Spanish: swords, batons, cups, coins. Ranks: Rey(12), Caballo(11), Sota(10), 7-2, As(1)."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "40-card pack, 12 stones (2 distinct) for scoring."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal and play anticlockwise. One suit = trump per deal."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
